{"id":"n1-138","title":"Verb ないではおかない","romaji":"~ nai de wa okanai","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Means 'cannot help but do', 'will definitely do', or 'is bound to happen'.","longExplanation":"The pattern Verb ないではおかない indicates that something definitely occurs as a logical or emotional consequence. It can be translated as 'cannot not do', 'can’t help but do', or 'will inevitably do'. The verb is put in the negative form followed by ないではおかない.","formation":"Verb-ない form + ではおかない","examples":[{"jp":"彼女は毎回遅刻をしては、先生に怒られないではおかない。","romaji":"Kanojo wa maikai chikoku o shite wa, sensei ni okorarenaide wa okanai.","en":"Every time she's late, she inevitably gets scolded by the teacher.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"毎回","vocabId":"1524670","reading":"まいかい"},{"surface":"遅刻","vocabId":"1422050","reading":"ちこく"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"先生","vocabId":"1387990","reading":"せんせい"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"怒ら","vocabId":"1445690","reading":"おこら","baseForm":"怒る"},{"surface":"れ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"れる"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"おか","vocabId":"1588920","reading":"おか","baseForm":"おく"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[14,15,16,17]},{"jp":"美味しいものがあれば、彼は食べないではおかない。","romaji":"Oishii mono ga areba, kare wa tabenai de wa okanai.","en":"If there's delicious food, he can't help but eat it.","words":[{"surface":"美味しい","vocabId":"1486650","reading":"おいしい"},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あれ","vocabId":"1857320","reading":"あれ","baseForm":"ある"},{"surface":"ば","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"su